      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO SUBJECT–VERB AGREEMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A verb must always agree with its subject in number (singular/plural) and person.",
        "Two singular subjects joined by 'and' take a plural verb, unless they represent a single concept or person.",
        "For subjects joined by 'either...or' or 'neither...nor', the verb agrees with the nearest subject.",
        "Collective nouns take a singular verb when acting as a unified whole, but a plural verb when individual members act separately.",
        "'A number of' is followed by a plural verb, whereas 'The number of' requires a singular verb."
      ],
      "id": "4u1r46y"
    },
